# LEGACY-RME-STEADY-STATE-OPS-1 — steady-state operations

## The operating model

Legacy RME migration is **routine production operations**. It is not an
engineering wave per batch, and a batch does not need a sprint.

A **routine batch** is the existing ROLL-4 wave record — never a new table, state
machine or lifecycle. A second path to the same clinical writes would be a weaker
one.

A batch is routine only if **all** hold: explicitly approved (fresh reference) ·
branch-scoped (named codes) · quota-bounded · time-bounded · maker/checker
assigned · source documents frozen · reconciliation required for closure.

## Non-negotiables

- **`ROLL-4-WAVE-3` remains SKIPPED / NOT REQUIRED.** Never create a Wave-3
  record, approval, quota or tag. Declaring it as a batch code is **refused** —
  it has no approval record and never will.
- **Every routine batch needs a FRESH approval.** Wave-1 and Wave-2R approvals are
  immutable historical evidence and are never reused.
- **Production resting state:** capability **OFF** · admission **EMPTY** · active
  batch **NONE**. A batch opens the minimum controls and returns to rest.
- **A routine batch never earns a GO tag.** GO tags are for software and
  governance changes that went through CI. A batch produces operational evidence
  and an approval closure.
- **No backup, no batch.** A verified backup under 24 h old is a refusal
  condition, not a warning.
- **Closure requires a balanced ledger:** zero in-flight, zero unexplained, zero
  quota drift, zero unresolved failures, plus a written sign-off. There is no
  `--force`.
- **A cancelled import still consumes quota.** Quota counts what was accepted into
  staging. Never read a quota total as a count of published documents.
- **Archive-only, permanently.** A legacy import never creates a ClinicVisit,
  native MedicalRecord, odontogram, prescription, invoice, payment, LabOrder or
  SATUSEHAT activity. Any such side effect is stop-the-line.
- **Never direct SQL or Tinker** for lifecycle state. Use
  `legacy-rme:import-admin` (dry-run first). A hand-edited row is an unaudited
  transition.
- **Never a shared maker/checker account.** One accountable human, one attributable
  account. Account separation is server-enforced; **human** separation is a human
  attestation the application cannot observe and must never imply it verified.

## Multi-branch

```
MULTI_BRANCH_MODE = CONCURRENT_BRANCH_ISOLATED_WITHIN_ONE_ACTIVE_BATCH
```

- **Across batches: SEQUENTIAL.** `LegacyRmeWaveBindingService` resolves one
  operative batch from one declared code. Do not claim or add concurrent batches.
- **Within one batch: CONCURRENT, BRANCH-ISOLATED.** Many branches, each with its
  own status, quota, operators and pause/drain/complete.

## Sizing

| Bound | Value |
|---|---|
| Routine default / day | 25 (the queue's single-worker pending ceiling) |
| Routine maximum / day | 100 (4× ceiling; human review is the constraint) |
| Above 100 | not routine — elevated approval required |
| Absolute rail | 500 (`max_declarable_daily`, server-side) |

**Measured throughput is NOT YET AVAILABLE** (five production documents total).
These are bounded defaults for recoverability, not a benchmark. Do not quote them
as measured.

## The pre-flight

`php artisan legacy-rme:ops-readiness` — read-only; opens, writes and repairs
nothing. Composes the deployment gate, operations layer, SOD posture, clinical
calendar, admission/approval, batch binding and window, sizing, reconciliation,
queue headroom and backup freshness into one decision, plus a branch matrix.

- Monitoring signals are collected **by default** (that is what establishes backup
  freshness). `--skip-monitoring` degrades honestly to NO_GO.
- `UNKNOWN` blocks exactly like `FAIL`. "We could not tell" is never a basis for
  opening a clinical migration.
- Exit `1` on NO_GO always; on WATCH only under `--strict` / `--fail-on-warning`.

## When extending this module

- **Compose, never duplicate.** Adding a second reader of an existing rule is the
  defect, not the feature. Read SOD through `SeparatePublisherGuard::enabled()`,
  never through its config key — an architecture test enforces that the switch has
  exactly one home in `app/`.
- **Guard every check** so it degrades to `UNKNOWN`, never to a silent GO.
- **PII-free output**: counts, branch codes, batch codes, statuses, account ids and
  timings. Never a patient name, Nomor RM, KTP/NIK, filename or document path. Never
  echo the approval reference — report its presence.
- **Distinguish "not established" from "failed".** Reporting an unchecked condition
  as a failed control trains operators to ignore the loudest signal.
- **A deliberately closed branch is `NOT_READY` with zero blockers**, not a fault.

